# Advanced settings for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on two CMP 170HX cards.
#
# You almost certainly don't need anything here: the common settings are in
# .env.example. ./start.sh reads only .env, so to use a setting from this
# file, copy its line into your .env (not into this file) and uncomment it.
# Every line shows the default the scripts use when it is unset, so a later
# release's new defaults reach you on ./start.sh update without editing .env.
# Delete or re-comment a line to go back to the default. The paths
# (/path/to/...) and HF_TOKEN lines are placeholders, not defaults; the note
# above each says what the default is.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, notes on their own lines starting with #.
# An unquoted value ends at the first " #" (whitespace then #), and a trailing
# "  (...)" (two or more spaces, then a note in parentheses) is dropped too.
# Quote the value, "..." or '...', to keep everything between the quotes.
# A prefix env assignment overrides .env for every key, including an
# explicit empty (KEY= ./start.sh):   MAX_SEQS=4 ./start.sh restart
#
# === engine pin =========================================================
# Left commented so a `git pull` of this repo can move the pin; ./start.sh
# installs the new engine when it changes. Uncomment to freeze the engine.
# A prefix assignment (IMAGE=... ./start.sh update) lasts for that run only.
#
# Container: the engine image, by digest.
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx@sha256:{{IMAGE_DIGEST}}
#
# Native: the vLLM fork and the commit it is pinned to. Each pin stays
# installable after the fork's branch moves on: it is kept under a
# qwen38-recipe-<version> tag.
# VLLM_COMMIT={{PIN}}
# VLLM_REPO=https://github.com/Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx.git
# VLLM_BRANCH=ampere
# Upstream nightly wheel that supplies the compiled extensions (native only).
# Unset: this release's wheel for this release's pin, otherwise the wheel of
# the pin's upstream base.
# VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_COMMIT=
# === paths ==============================================================
# Give an ABSOLUTE path when you move one. MODELS_DIR is in .env.example.
# Default: venv/ in this repo.
# VENV=/path/to/venv
# Default: vllm-src/ in this repo.
# VLLM_SRC=/path/to/vllm-src
# Default: MODELS_DIR/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-exl3. Must be on an SSD.
# MODEL=/path/to/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-exl3
# CUDA toolkit root. Triton and the EXL3 build use it.
# CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.3
#
# Weights to download: the repository and the pinned revision of its 5.05 bpw branch.
# TARGET_REPO=turboderp/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-exl3
# TARGET_REVISION={{CHECKPOINT_REVISION}}
# Unauthenticated Hub downloads are rate limited; a token is faster.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# 1 re-fetches the weights even when the files are already there.
# REFRESH_WEIGHTS=0
# === serving limits =====================================================
# Context is fixed at 262144 and GPU memory at 0.95: serve.sh refuses others.
# Concurrent sequences.
# MAX_SEQS=8
# Parsers for Qwen's reasoning blocks and tool calls.
# REASONING_PARSER=qwen3
# TOOL_PARSER=qwen3_coder
# Extra vLLM arguments, whitespace-separated. Options that change the
# deployment (parallelism, dtype, context, graphs, speculation) are refused.
# EXTRA_ARGS=
# Seconds to wait for /health after launch.
# READY_TIMEOUT=1800
# 1 runs the post-start check (two requests, drafting active) after health.
# BOOT_CHECK=1
# Seconds stop waits for a clean shutdown.
# STOP_TIMEOUT=120
# === speculative decoding ===============================================
# mtp (native MTP drafter inside the checkpoint) or none.
# SPEC_MODE=mtp
# Draft tokens per step.
# SPEC_N=3
# 1: each card takes the argmax over its half of the vocabulary for drafts and
# gathers (value, index) pairs instead of full draft logits; same drafts.
# LOCAL_ARGMAX=0
# === scheduler ==========================================================
# Tokens per scheduler step (prefill chunk plus decode slots).
# MAX_BATCHED=3460
# === n-gram (PLE) table ==================================================
# Where the n-gram table lives: ssd (default: read rows from the checkpoint
# file), or ram / device (comparison placements, not the tested default).
# PLE_PLACEMENT=ssd
# === container ==========================================================
# CONTAINER_NAME=qwen38-flash-next
# SHM_SIZE=16g
# Default: cache/ in this repo.
# CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache
# === install / build ====================================================
# Preflight limits (read only).
# MIN_GPUS=2
# MIN_GPU_MIB=61440
# NEED_DISK_GB=120
# 1 compiles upstream's CUDA extensions instead of using its nightly wheel.
# BUILD_FROM_SOURCE=0
# MAX_JOBS=16
# 1 keeps completed native install steps on a retry.
# NATIVE_INSTALL_RESUME=1
# FLASHINFER_INSTALL_ATTEMPTS=3
# FLASHINFER_HTTP_TIMEOUT=30
# FLASHINFER_INSTALL_TIMEOUT=600
# === engine switches (kill switches: set 0 and restart) =================
# Canonical sparse-attention top-k ties: a request repeats at exact score ties.
# VLLM_QWEN4_QSA_TOPK_CANONICAL=1
# Flags-in-data two-shot custom all-reduce for the TP2 all-reduces it covers.
# VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_FLAGS=1
# PLE row reads overlap the previous decoder layer instead of stalling the step.
# VLLM_EXL3_PLE_OVERLAP=1
# EXL3 MoE kernel v2 for MoE calls of 1-64 rows (decode and short prefills).
# VLLM_EXL3_MOE_V2=1
# EXL3 split-K dense kernel for the small-row decode launches.
# VLLM_EXL3_DENSE_SPLITK=1
# Custom all-reduce over PCIe peer access (applies only after the P2P check passes).
# VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_PCIE_P2P=1
# NCCL over peer access (applies only after the P2P check passes).
# NCCL_P2P_LEVEL=SYS
# Allocator: custom all-reduce needs legacy CUDA IPC handles.
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False
# Opt-in device-specific compilation cache seed (container only).
# VLLM_IMAGE_CACHE_SEED=0
